rogram over the function's own file: same-module helpers are code — `cone`, `members`), ALONE when the cone does not lower. MEASURED on our code: df.stmts, expr.of, clones.blocks all `outside` (a module-local alias, a field write, a required module) — the proof covers self-contained code today. CART-1445 |\n| SPECIALIZE any function to some of its arguments — and is the residual still the same function? | `toolbelt.lua run specialize <dir> ref=<file::name> statics='{\"n\": 3}' samples='[[2], [5]]'` — mixfn (lower, with the cone) -> mix.specialize -> mix.print -> load -> ACCEPT against mix.run (the original, mix's own evaluator) on every sample: the residual text, mix's stats, per sample both values. A refusal is mix's located one (`goto_statement (not in S) — at line 1`). The pipeline compile_match runs for the matcher, for any function in mix's subset. CART-1445 |","file":".claude/skills/cartograph/references/questions.md","before":"| MEMOIZE a function — wrap it so a repeated argument answers from a memo, with the residence chosen? | `toolbelt.lua run memoize <dir> ref=<file::name> residence=weak|strong|generation [generation=<Lua expr>] apply=1` — ONE ground edit at the header: the body becomes `NAME_raw`, the header a wrapper (nil / NaN arguments bypass; several parameters key a nested memo, a method keys `self` first; EVERY result kept — nil, multiple values). weak = by argument identity (a scalar key is never collected), strong = the process, generation = cleared when the expression changes (read after the nil guard; it may index a parameter: `store.generation`). No `residence` = the `memo-residence` DECISION (a gated edit). Refuses by name: non-Lua, varargs, no parameter, a header that is not `function NAME(…)`. Purity / unshared results are NOT established — the optimize loop's A/B tests them. CART-1444 |"},"touched":[".claude/skills/cartograph/references/questions.md"],"verb":"edit"},"bytes":2663,"decided_by":"tactic","decisions":[],"id":"1791167827.564808-